"""Build a portable result report from accepted native outputs only."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
s=json.loads((B/'results/summary.json').read_text())
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>R-{i+1:02d}</td><td>{q:.2f}</td><td>{s["flow_target_rack_Lmin"]:.2f}</td><td>{s["supply_pressure_absolute_kPa"][i]:.2f}</td><td>{s["return_pressure_absolute_kPa"][i]:.2f}</td></tr>' for i,q in enumerate(s['rack_flow_Lmin']))
a=s['numerical_audits'];ind=s['independent_colebrook_check']
cards=''.join(f'<article><span>{name}</span><strong>{value}</strong></article>' for name,value in [('Total flow',f'{s["total_flow_Lps"]:.2f} L/s'),('Pump head',f'{s["pump_head_m"]:.2f} m'),('Pump differential',f'{s["pump_dp_kPa"]:.1f} kPa'),('Estimated electric input',f'{s["electrical_power_W"]/1000:.2f} kW')])
doc=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>First OpenModelica hydraulic network | Khani Solutions</title><style>*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;background:#f0f5f7;color:#17394d;font:16px/1.65 system-ui}}main{{max-width:1250px;margin:auto;padding:30px 22px}}h1{{font-size:38px;line-height:1.2}}h2{{font-size:24px;line-height:1.3}}.eyebrow{{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:750}}.note{{background:#fff5dc;border-left:4px solid #bd913a;padding:15px 20px}}.cards{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:16px;margin:25px 0}}article,.panel{{padding:20px;background:white;border:1px solid #d6e3e9;border-radius:10px}}article span,article strong{{display:block}}article strong{{font-size:26px}}article span{{font-size:13px;color:#557080}}img{{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;background:white}}.panel{{margin:24px 0;overflow-x:auto}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}}td,th{{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #dae4e9;text-align:left}}a{{color:#086f95}}.downloads{{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}}.downloads a{{background:#17394d;color:white;padding:10px 15px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none}}.small{{font-size:13px;color:#557080}}code{{font-size:13px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}}@media(max-width:750px){{.cards{{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}h1{{font-size:29px}}}}@media(max-width:420px){{.cards{{grid-template-columns:1fr}}}}</style><main><p class="eyebrow">KHANI SOLUTIONS / DATA-CENTER COOLING / STAGE 03</p><h1>The first solved hydraulic network.</h1><p>Ten parallel rack branches, segmented direct-return headers, measured CAD routes and an explicit equivalent curve for two duty pumps. Built and solved on Intel with OpenModelica 1.27.1 and Modelica Standard Library 4.1.0.</p><p class="note">Initial steady numerical study with assumed device curves and fitting losses. The 1 MW heat load sets the flow target; rack heating, physical heat-exchanger thermal performance, controls and startup are not simulated.</p><div class="cards">{cards}</div><p>Each duty pump carries approximately <strong>{s['flow_per_duty_pump_m3h']:.2f} m³/h</strong>. The standby is isolated. Rack flow ranges from <strong>{min(s['rack_flow_Lmin']):.2f} to {max(s['rack_flow_Lmin']):.2f} L/min</strong>, versus a 144.7 L/min nominal thermal-duty target. The flow spread is {s['flow_spread_percent_of_mean']:.2f}% of the mean.</p><div class="panel"><img src="results/hydraulic-baseline.png" alt="Native rack flow and header pressure results, the assumed pump curve with solved operating point, and the lowest-flow rack pressure budget"><p class="small">OpenModelica numerical outputs; the orange comparison points use an independent exact-Colebrook network calculation with the same assumptions. These are steady operating-point plots, not a time-dependent startup response.</p></div><section class="panel"><h2>Read the network, step by step</h2><ol><li>Convert the 1 MW / 10 K design basis into the target flow using fixed water properties near 40 °C.</li><li>Import routed lengths; exclude the two 0.6 m blind header tails from circulating flow.</li><li>Intersect the explicit assumed pump curve with flow-dependent network resistance. Flow is solved, not forced to the thermal target. The Stage 01 pressure margin is a selection allowance, not an extra physical resistor.</li><li>Reduce supply-header flow as racks branch off; accumulate return flow toward the CDU.</li><li>Include hydrostatic pressure changes across risers, rack drops and returns. Each complete equal-density closed loop has zero net static head.</li><li>Check mass and pressure balances, then compare against an independent network solution before interpreting the distribution.</li></ol><p>The near racks receive slightly more flow because their shared header paths are shorter. All rack flows exceed the initial target with this curve. A later control stage can test reduced speed and balancing; this run does not optimize them.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Rack operating points</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Rack</th><th>Flow, L/min</th><th>Target, L/min</th><th>Supply absolute, kPa</th><th>Return absolute, kPa</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></section><section class="panel"><h2>Numerical verification</h2><ul><li>Equation check: {s['model_equations']:,} equations and variables.</li><li>Maximum mass-balance residual: {a['max_mass_residual_kg_s']:.2e} kg/s.</li><li>Maximum loop-pressure residual: {a['max_loop_pressure_residual_Pa']:.2e} Pa.</li><li>Independent Colebrook comparison: maximum rack-flow difference {ind['max_flow_difference_percent']:.4f}%.</li><li>Flat and 3.0 m header checks preserve flow and pump head at fixed friction lengths; local pressures shift by the expected hydrostatic amount. The raised check stays within available pipe lengths.</li><li>The numerical fixed-temperature volume removes pump work to close the model energy equations. It is not an expansion-vessel size or physical CDU thermal prediction.</li></ul><details><summary>Retained compiler note and acceptance limits</summary><p>{html.escape(' '.join(s['warnings_retained']))}</p><p>The accepted run has no unit inconsistency, negative-height bound warning or runtime assertion failure. The algebraic solution is repeated over 0–1 s for CSV export; this does not simulate startup. No physical validation, selected pump/NPSHR curve, pressure qualification, water hammer, control dynamics or standby switchover is established.</p></details></section><section class="panel"><h2>Reproduce and inspect</h2><p class="downloads"><a href="Stage-03-Hydraulics-R1.zip" download>Complete model and results</a><a href="model/DataCenterHydraulics.mo" download>Native Modelica package</a><a href="results/rack-results.csv" download>Rack results CSV</a><a href="results/summary.json" download>Checks and assumptions JSON</a></p><p>Open <code>model/DataCenterHydraulics.mo</code> in OMEdit, load Modelica 4.1.0 and simulate <code>DataCenterHydraulics.Baseline</code>. See README.txt for command-line reproduction and the scope of the equivalent components.</p></section><p class="small">Mohammadreza Khani, PhD · Independent numerical study · 23 October 2026 · Next: review the baseline, then test speed, balancing and component sensitivities.</p></main></html>'''
(B/'Report.html').write_text(doc)
print('Built first hydraulic result report.')
